(SHORE STAFF LEAVE POLICY \(DOC HR-POL-01, REV 2.0\)) Tj
0 -15 Td
() Tj
0 -15 Td
(1. Scope, Eligibility, and Probation Period) Tj
0 -15 Td
(This policy applies to all full-time and part-time permanent shore staff based at) Tj
0 -15 Td
(regional port offices in Rotterdam, Singapore, Hamburg, and Busan.) Tj
0 -15 Td
(Offshore vessel crew, harbor pilots, and external contractors follow separate) Tj
0 -15 Td
(maritime collective agreements and are excluded from this handbook.) Tj
0 -15 Td
(Every newly hired shore employee completes a 90-calendar-day probation period) Tj
0 -15 Td
(starting on their official hire date. Manager confirmation on day 80 converts the) Tj
0 -15 Td
(appointment to confirmed shore status.) Tj
0 -15 Td
(Part-time shore staff working at least 20 hours per week receive pro-rated leave) Tj
0 -15 Td
(entitlements proportional to their contracted weekly hours / 40.) Tj
0 -15 Td
() Tj
0 -15 Td
(2. Annual Leave Entitlement and Monthly Accrual) Tj
0 -15 Td
(Confirmed full-time shore staff accrue paid annual leave based on completed) Tj
0 -15 Td
(continuous service: 21 working days per calendar year \(1.75 days/month\) for 0 to 3) Tj
0 -15 Td
(years of tenure; 24 working days per calendar year \(2.00 days/month\) after 3) Tj
0 -15 Td
(completed years; and 26 working days per calendar year \(2.17 days/month\) after 7) Tj
0 -15 Td
(completed years.) Tj
0 -15 Td
(During the initial 90-calendar-day probation period, annual leave accrues on paper) Tj
0 -15 Td
(at 1.75 days per month but paid annual leave cannot be scheduled or taken until) Tj
0 -15 Td
(day 91, except during mandatory local port holiday closures.) Tj
0 -15 Td
(In hire or separation years, entitlement is pro-rated by calendar months served) Tj
0 -15 Td
(and rounded to the nearest 0.5 working day. Unpaid sabbaticals exceeding 15) Tj
0 -15 Td
(working days halt accrual proportionally.) Tj
0 -15 Td
(Cross-policy rule: monthly annual leave accrual pauses immediately during any) Tj
0 -15 Td
(unpaid administrative suspension exceeding 5 working days imposed under the Shore) Tj
0 -15 Td
(Staff Code of Conduct \(DOC HR-POL-02, Section 8\).) Tj
0 -15 Td
() Tj
0 -15 Td
(3. Annual Leave Carry-Over, Expiry, and Separation Payout) Tj
0 -15 Td
(Up to 5 unused annual leave days may carry over from one calendar year into Q1 of) Tj
0 -15 Td
(the following year and expire permanently on March 31 at 17:30 local time if not) Tj
0 -15 Td
(taken.) Tj
0 -15 Td
(Unused days exceeding the 5-day carry-over cap are forfeited on December 31 unless) Tj
0 -15 Td
(a Vice President \(VP\) grants a written operational-freeze deferral \(for example) Tj
0 -15 Td
(during a vessel dry-dock emergency\), extending expiry to June 30.) Tj
0 -15 Td
(Shore staff may not cash out unused annual leave during active employment. Upon) Tj
0 -15 Td
(resignation or termination, accrued unused leave is paid out at base daily salary) Tj
0 -15 Td
(\(annual base salary divided by 260 working days\).) Tj
0 -15 Td
(If a departing employee has a negative annual leave balance approved in an) Tj
0 -15 Td
(emergency, up to 3 negative days may be deducted from the final settlement.) Tj
0 -15 Td
